  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&#xbf;s Economic Empowerment in Uzbekistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The Action aims to create an inclusive economic environment where women can thrive. This involves dismantling deep-rooted gender biases and societal norms which limit women&apos;s opportunities and potential. By promoting gender equality in the workplace, enhancing access to education and vocational training, supporting women&apos;s entrepreneurship, as well as enhancing family planning services, the Action will empower women to secure decent work and grow their businesses. This will boost their economic independence and contribute significantly to Uzbekistan&apos;s overall economic growth and social development. Through targeted interventions and comprehensive support, the Action will foster a culture that values and utilizes the full potential of women in the economy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall objective&lt;/strong&gt; (Impact): Women equally participate in the economy and labour force of Uzbekistan without being affected by gender stereotypes and harmful social norms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific objective&lt;/strong&gt; (Outcome) 1: Women in the target regions, including women with disabilities, have improved access to enabling services, resources, and opportunities for decent work, entrepreneurship, and economic participation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific objective&lt;/strong&gt; (Outcome) 2: Positive shifts in societal perceptions of gender stereotypes and harmful social norms contribute to the realization of women&#xbf;s rights and increased participation of women in the workforce.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific objective&lt;/strong&gt; (Outcome) 3: Women of reproductive age have equitable access to a full range of modern family planning methods at the primary health care level, based on evidence-informed planning and service delivery.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
